<title>FRANCE: Revised figures confirm French Q2 GDP fell 0.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Revised figures confirm French Q2 GDP fell 0.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics office INSEE gave the following gross domestic product data (base 1980, changes from previous quarters in percent except stocks variation, in billions of 1980 francs.)</p>
<p>					 Q2	 Q1</p>
<p> Total GDP			  -0.4	1.1</p>
<p> Imports			    -0.8	1.6</p>
<p> Exports			    -2.0	3.5</p>
<p> Household consumption	  -0.8	2.4</p>
<p> Investment			 -0.6     -0.1</p>
<p> Stocks variation		 -4.7     -9.3</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following more detailed breakdown:</p>
<p>				Q2 96  Q1 96  Q4 95  Q3 95  Q2 95   1995</p>
<p> Total GDP		  -0.4    1.1    -0.4   0.2    0.1     0.6</p>
<p> Imports		    -0.8    1.6    -2.2   1.0    0.1     1.9</p>
<p> Exports		    -2.0    3.5    -0.9  -1.3    0.1     2.9</p>
<p> Household consumption  -0.8    2.4    -0.3   0.0    1.6    -0.2</p>
<p> Public consumption	0.5    0.5     0.4   0.4    0.1     0.2</p>
<p> Investment		 -0.6   -0.1    -0.3   1.8   -2.3     1.2</p>
<p>  - business investment -1.4    1.0    -1.3   1.9   -2.2     1.3</p>
<p>  - household investment 1.3   -0.5     1.0   1.6   -2.4     2.6</p>
<p>  - public investment   -1.0   -4.4     0.4   1.7   -3.2    -0.5</p>
<p> Stocks variation	 -4.7   -9.3    -0.2   5.9    2.8     5.6</p>
<p> Internal demand	   0.0    0.6    -0.8   0.8    0.1     0.3</p>
<p>INSEE noted that so-called &quot;acquired growth&quot; for 1996 -- the annual growth that would be recorded if there were no change in growth for the rest of the year -- was 0.6 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
</text>
